    "notes": {
      "Prendel3/Moon 2": "E5M2 and E6M4 stage a base and three Galors at 6100-6368 GU, just past Moon 2's authored set-local position (400, 5000, 0) -- per the design doc this body should be a PIN so the layout can never move it away from that staged content. NOT declared as an active overrides.pins entry here: verified empirically (--check, both with the offset temporarily zeroed AND restored to the authored (400, 5000, 0)) that engine/systems/validate.py's pin-respected rule reports a problem EITHER way -- restored, it reports the body sitting at set-local (8790.27, 42574.95, 0) relative to the region anchor, ~38500 GU from the authored offset, not a rounding gap. Root cause: tools/systems/layout.py places every region's companion bodies at `primary_radius * (moon_first_orbit_factor + moon_orbit_step_factor * j)` from the primary -- direction preserved, absolute distance intentionally discarded (see the module docstring and _standoff_factor) -- and layout() never reads overrides.pins at all (only gen_system_maps.pins_from() does, and only to hand validate() a value to check post-hoc). So no data-only override can make this pin hold; it needs layout() to special-case a pinned body by placing it at anchor + pin_offset after the regular placement pass, which is a tools/ code change outside this data-only task's scope. Left unpinned rather than shipping a pin declaration the validator itself proves false -- see the Task 7 report for the full derivation and a concrete fix sketch."
